                <pb facs="0869" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.6363/146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-08T17:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>200. Your 271, December 8, 9 a.m. In the light of information from London Embassy
                    regarding conversations held in British Foreign Office, the Department does not
                    understand issuance to Clive of this instruction at this stage. Department will
                    expect to inform and instruct you early next week. Meanwhile, take no action
                    except to inform Clive of the foregoing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
